text:
maria: FYI linkbot just flagged several examples in the function/tool-calling page that still point at the old SDK. I'm going to open a docs PR unless someone else is on it. :eyes:

sam: I can take it. I'll update the snippets to the new SDK call shape and add a short migration note for legacy users. planning to keep an explicit shim example.

eli: +1. please include a tiny backwards-compat shim (1-2 lines) so folks can copy/paste. also add one compact example showing structured output parsing with a nullable field.

ben: One thing I noticed earlier — the current JSON example in the guide omits the required `tool` property in the sample envelope. That caused our parser tests to be noisy. Can you fix that sample and add a unit test?

sam: ack. branch coming up: `docs/fncall-sdk-migration`. snippet I'll swap from the old `invokeTool()` to the new `redwood.calls.invoke()` pattern. putting quick diff here:

```js
// old (in docs)
const res = await invokeTool('search', { q: 'cats' })
// new (replacement)
const res = await redwood.calls.invoke({
  tool: 'search',
  input: { q: 'cats' },
})
// shim for legacy users (optional)
function invokeTool(name, input) {
  return redwood.calls.invoke({ tool: name, input })
}
```

maria: Nice. can you also run the link-checker after you push? linkbot will re-scan and we should fix any redirects. I'll schedule the PR review once linkbot is clean.

linkbot: Scanned 5 pages in /docs/function-calling and /docs/structured-output — found 3 broken links: /docs/old-toolcalls -> 404, /examples/old-sdk-snippet -> 404, /images/schema-v1.png -> 410. Suggested action: add redirects and update inline links.

ben: tiny nit: prefer `redwood.calls.invoke` to accept named args as you showed (makes diffs cleaner). Also update the JSON schema example to show "tool": "search" explicitly and mark `results` nullable ("results": {"type": ["array","null"]})

sam: got it. I'll patch the schema sample, add a short migration section at the top, and add a docs CI check for 404s (so link-checker runs on PR). pushing in a few. :thumbsup:

maria: great — tag me when the PR is up. I'll add a short blurb to the release notes and coordinate a small docs deploy during the next window.

eli: thanks! also can we add an example of parsing an envelope where `metadata` is optional? that helped one customer avoid a crash. small snippet like:

```json
{"tool":"search","input":{"q":"x"},"metadata":null}
```

sam: will include that. PR expected in ~30m, ping me here if you want me to tweak wording.

maria: perfect, thanks team.
